    {
      "key": "3ae152a9-00e3-4d63-8eb0-7ceef3e1b625",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-file-text-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Distribute:** Give each student a copy of the Rubric - Variables Make"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "3ae152a9-00e3-4d63-8eb0-7ceef3e1b625",
        "lesson_activity.key": "3da87dbc-e1ef-46dd-a3e1-351eb93e0bf9"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "3ccb13e6-3c36-42c2-ba74-266765ac6804",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students plan a personally meaningful scene by labeling five variables (three strings, one int, one bool), then bring that plan to life in code, handing off to the AI Tutor to generate the visual.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 14, Level 1 to complete levels 1-2.\n- **Level 1:** Students place five color-coded label boxes onto a sketch (three string, one int, one bool), then draw arrows connecting each label to its part of the scene.\n- **Level 2:** Students turn their sketch into variables (**input()** for the **strings**, direct assignment for the **int** and **bool**), reassign one, and print them all. The AI Tutor then builds the visual from their code and sketch, which students predict, run, and evaluate before documenting what they kept, changed, or rejected.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** By roughly the 10-minute mark, most students should be moving from Level 1 into Level 2 — flag anyone still finalizing their sketch well past that point. In Level 2, check that string variables use input() and that the int/bool do not, and confirm the reassignment line updates a variable already created above it, not a brand-new variable. For the AI Tutor step, watch for students running before predicting, redirect them to write a prediction first.",
        "duration": "35",
        "name": "Plan, Then Build",
        "progression_name": "Sketch and Make",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Students may try to use **input()** for their int and bool variables. If asked why those two don't use **input()**, explain that **input()** always returns text: a value like 5 would be stored as the string \"5\" rather than the number 5. Working around this is covered in a later lesson."
          },
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "Use this level to check whether students can correctly assign variables by type, reassign a variable's value, and evaluate and document AI-generated code against their own design."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "3ccb13e6-3c36-42c2-ba74-266765ac6804",
        "lesson_activity.key": "3da87dbc-e1ef-46dd-a3e1-351eb93e0bf9"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "48a99318-21ce-4c6c-9a1d-e10da7d80a1e",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the lesson objectives."
      },
