    {
      "key": "38585b73-021e-46b5-a164-bfcc6698be23",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** Click the animated slide to display the discussion prompts.\n- *What was awesome about writing your code?*\n- *What is one action you can take to improve your code?*\n- *What questions do you have about today?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:**  : Students reflect on how they used randint() to create random effects in their Theater scene. Listen for students to describe what they randomized, how their number ranges affected the result, and what they would revise to make the scene feel more intentional.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Glows, Grows, Want-to-Knows helps students celebrate progress, name a next step, and surface questions or misconceptions before moving on."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
