    {
      "key": "852663f1-e203-44ca-9db2-e2aeede2a58d",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "duration": "5",
        "name": "Warm Up"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "852663f1-e203-44ca-9db2-e2aeede2a58d",
        "lesson_activity.key": "176ede1c-03a5-4bf8-9e35-71f242194068"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "1b9accc3-1d0b-4b7f-a01a-3548bab0678e",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students connect the cultural \"wrapped\"-style recap format they already recognize to the idea that good personalization comes from specific, meaningful details, not just a name slapped on a template — setting up the \"who is it for, and why\" question they'll answer in Level 1.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** Click the animated slide to display the discussion prompts.\n- *What's an example of a \"wrapped\"-style recap you've seen?*\n- *What made it feel personal instead of generic, not just labeled with a name?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students name a specific personalization detail —not a generic \"it had my name on it\" — that connects to the \"who is it for, and why\" question they'll answer in Level 1's Topic step."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "1b9accc3-1d0b-4b7f-a01a-3548bab0678e",
        "lesson_activity.key": "176ede1c-03a5-4bf8-9e35-71f242194068"
      }
    },
